>> "  TEST 1 — tui/05_key_input.zy" ¶
>> "  What it does => reads a single keypress (<<|)" ¶
>> "  How to test  => press any key when prompted" ¶
>> "  Expected     => the pressed key name is printed, then newline" ¶
>> "" ¶
>> "───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" ¶
>> "  TEST 2 — tui/06_tui_block.zy" ¶
>> "  What it does => enters alternate screen (>>| block), prints 'tui', exits" ¶
>> "  How to test  => observe the terminal switches to alternate screen" ¶
>> "  Expected     => alternate screen shows 'tui', then terminal returns to normal" ¶
>> "" ¶
>> "───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" ¶
>> "  TEST 3 — tui/07_output_pos_sparse.zy" ¶
>> "  What it does => positions output at screen row=1 col=1 (>>~ syntax)" ¶
>> "  How to test  => 'A' should appear at top-left of terminal" ¶
>> "  Expected     => ESC[1;1H cursor move followed by 'A'" ¶
>> "" ¶
